Test rg55: literals whose values are all known, numbered wrongly by the pool key
// Every value each literal reads is known where it is written, so its pool key is
// hashExpr()'s number, meant to be its value.  Where evalExpr() gives another value
// (-0 folds to 0; a negative operand of + or *), literals of different values once
// shared one pool word, and all but the first loaded a wrong value.  zero is a label
// at 0, defined first.  The comment on each line is the word its literal must load.
0/
zero,   0
100/
    lac [-0]            // 000000
    lac [~0]            // 777777
    lac [-zero]         // 000000
    lac [~zero]         // 777777
    lac [0]             // 000000
    lac [-1+2]          // 000001
    lac [-2*3]          // 777771
    lac [-10]           // 777767
    hlt
    constants
stop
